\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {What the play is not.} (\textbf  {a}) Cooperation by round with 95\% bootstrap bands. Three of four models decay towards the endgame, consistent with backward induction; Claude is the exception, rising from 0.47 to 0.74. Gemini is the single arm that was told the round count. (\textbf  {b}) The memory-one fingerprint: probability of cooperating after each joint outcome of the previous round, the complete description of a memory-one strategy. Dashes mark tit-for-tat. All four cooperate readily after being exploited (CD), where every canonical rule except AllC prescribes 0, and three of four cooperate less after exploiting (DC) than after being exploited. (\textbf  {c}) How an archetype label is actually reached. Dark: exactly one of the 32 deterministic memory-one rules reproduces the whole trajectory. Mid: several do. Grey: none does, and the label is a nearest-neighbour statement. The right-hand column gives the mean number of rounds out of ten on which play departs from its own nearest rule.}}{9}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:strategy}{{3}{9}{\textbf {What the play is not.} (\textbf {a}) Cooperation by round with 95\% bootstrap bands. Three of four models decay towards the endgame, consistent with backward induction; Claude is the exception, rising from 0.47 to 0.74. Gemini is the single arm that was told the round count. (\textbf {b}) The memory-one fingerprint: probability of cooperating after each joint outcome of the previous round, the complete description of a memory-one strategy. Dashes mark tit-for-tat. All four cooperate readily after being exploited (CD), where every canonical rule except AllC prescribes 0, and three of four cooperate less after exploiting (DC) than after being exploited. (\textbf {c}) How an archetype label is actually reached. Dark: exactly one of the 32 deterministic memory-one rules reproduces the whole trajectory. Mid: several do. Grey: none does, and the label is a nearest-neighbour statement. The right-hand column gives the mean number of rounds out of ten on which play departs from its own nearest rule}{figure.caption.4}{}}
